From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muhammad Falak R Wani <falakreyaz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:35:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] vendor: cilium/ebpf: drop unused asm.Instructions.Tag

asm.Instructions.Tag is the only importer of crypto/sha1 in runc's
dependency graph. Nothing in runc or its vendored dependencies calls it
(opencontainers/cgroups only uses asm to assemble and marshal the
device-filter program), and the Go linker already discards it from the
runc binary. Removing it drops crypto/sha1 from the build graph so that
runc links no Go crypto packages at all.

Azure Linux-specific: Tag is public cilium/ebpf API (deprecated upstream
by https://github.com/cilium/ebpf/pull/1932 in favour of HasTag, which
uses both SHA-1 and SHA-256), so this is not suitable for upstream as-is.

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Falak R Wani <falakreyaz@gmail.com>
---
 .../github.com/cilium/ebpf/asm/instruction.go | 21 -------------------
 1 file changed, 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/cilium/ebpf/asm/instruction.go b/vendor/github.com/cilium/ebpf/asm/instruction.go
index 86b384c..c574f81 100644
--- a/vendor/github.com/cilium/ebpf/asm/instruction.go
+++ b/vendor/github.com/cilium/ebpf/asm/instruction.go
@@ -1,9 +1,7 @@
 package asm
 
 import (
-	"crypto/sha1"
 	"encoding/binary"
-	"encoding/hex"
 	"errors"
 	"fmt"
 	"io"
@@ -787,25 +785,6 @@ func (insns Instructions) Marshal(w io.Writer, bo binary.ByteOrder) error {
 	return nil
 }
 
-// Tag calculates the kernel tag for a series of instructions.
-//
-// It mirrors bpf_prog_calc_tag in the kernel and so can be compared
-// to ProgramInfo.Tag to figure out whether a loaded program matches
-// certain instructions.
-func (insns Instructions) Tag(bo binary.ByteOrder) (string, error) {
-	h := sha1.New()
-	for i, ins := range insns {
-		if ins.IsLoadFromMap() {
-			ins.Constant = 0
-		}
-		_, err := ins.Marshal(h, bo)
-		if err != nil {
-			return "", fmt.Errorf("instruction %d: %w", i, err)
-		}
-	}
-	return hex.EncodeToString(h.Sum(nil)[:sys.BPF_TAG_SIZE]), nil
-}
-
 // encodeFunctionReferences populates the Offset (or Constant, depending on
 // the instruction type) field of instructions with a Reference field to point
 // to the offset of the corresponding instruction with a matching Symbol field.
